If $W' \to W$ is birational, then the result follows from Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02RQ" data-tag="02RQ">42.18.2</a>. Our task is to show that even if $W' \to W$ has degree $> 1$ the basic rational equivalence $[W'_0]_ k \sim _{rat} [W'_\infty ]_ k$ comes from a principal divisor on a subvariety of $X$.